# A CONSTANT DIVISOR SELECTS A DIFFERENT ROW. `x / 7` and `x / d` mean the same
# thing and must answer the same, but they do not have to be the same C. A
# variable divisor goes through a helper that checks it for zero (and, for a
# signed type, for -1 under the minimum); a literal divisor that is neither
# needs no check, and its `const=` row divides inline.
#
# make const-row-guard reads the emitted C and pins both directions: each
# variable divisor calls the helper, and no constant one does. This fixture
# answers for the VALUES; the guard answers for the FORM.
main: function is {
    x: 100.u64
    d: 7.u64
    print "const divisor: \{x / 7} \{x % 7}"
    print "variable divisor: \{x / d} \{x % d}"

    s: (0.i16 - 100.i16)
    v: 3.i16
    print "signed const: \{s / 3} \{s % 3}"
    print "signed variable: \{s / v} \{s % v}"
}
